      "problem": "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A={-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}?$\n\n$min(A)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,max(A)=$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(A) & =min{-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}=-8 \\\\ max(A) & =max{-8,\\,0,\\,4,\\,-1}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
